{
  "case_id": "2004-03-1388",
  "document_hash": "3a0fc2b63b9ac03869965db16cacd030a9987871042851b9b41a4a7edf44a61c",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1388",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a0fc2b63b9ac03869965db16cacd030a9987871042851b9b41a4a7edf44a61c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a0fc2b63b9a-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nTHOMAS C. GOLDSTEIN, ESQ., Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Petitioners.\nDAVID B. SALMONS, ESQ., Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting the Petitioners.\nDAVID C. FREDERICK, ESQ., Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Respondent.\nGREGORY G. GARRE, ESQ., Washington, D.C.; on behalf of The Bahamas, as amicus curiae, supporting the Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1388",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a0fc2b63b9ac03869965db16cacd030a9987871042851b9b41a4a7edf44a61c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a0fc2b63b9a-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The petitioners in this case are American citizens who took cruises to and from this country on tickets bought here that call for the application of U.S. law. They were subject to discrimination by respondent, a U.S.-based company on the land, in the ports, and in the waters of the United States."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1388",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a0fc2b63b9ac03869965db16cacd030a9987871042851b9b41a4a7edf44a61c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a0fc2b63b9a-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE O'CONNOR: Mr. Goldstein, may I inquire of you whether other countries, for instance, in the EU area, have applied their own disability laws to some of the cruise ships that touch base in their courts?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1388",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a0fc2b63b9ac03869965db16cacd030a9987871042851b9b41a4a7edf44a61c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a0fc2b63b9a-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The first is that there has been a detailed rulemaking underway in which the regulatory authorities charged by Congress with implementing the ADA have spent quite some time. They have produced this single-spaced, half-inch thick document that is dedicated to making --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1388",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a0fc2b63b9ac03869965db16cacd030a9987871042851b9b41a4a7edf44a61c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a0fc2b63b9a-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Mr. Goldstein, may -- may I take it from your answer that it doesn't make any difference in your view, your answer to the question about the -- the ship leaving from a port in England and going many places and touching base in New York, that kind of a voyage, or what this case seems to be where the vast majority of the passengers are from the United States, the port of departure is in the United States, the port of return is in the United States. You don't seem to distinguish those cases because you say in the New York port, it doesn't matter if it's really a U.S.-centered cruise or a cruise centered in Italy or any place else. Is that correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1388",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a0fc2b63b9ac03869965db16cacd030a9987871042851b9b41a4a7edf44a61c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a0fc2b63b9a-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We're not questioning the authority. We're questioning whether Congress intended that to be the case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Goldstein",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1388",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a0fc2b63b9ac03869965db16cacd030a9987871042851b9b41a4a7edf44a61c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a0fc2b63b9a-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice Scalia, we disagree, and let me just take you to your cases. I did that, I think, in the Jones Act and the NLRA context."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1388",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a0fc2b63b9ac03869965db16cacd030a9987871042851b9b41a4a7edf44a61c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a0fc2b63b9a-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In other words, I'm trying to understand. You don't know what your position is --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Goldstein",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1388",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a0fc2b63b9ac03869965db16cacd030a9987871042851b9b41a4a7edf44a61c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a0fc2b63b9a-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We do believe it would be covered because the accommodation was purchased here, although we haven't raised the claim in this Court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "David B. Salmons",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1388",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a0fc2b63b9ac03869965db16cacd030a9987871042851b9b41a4a7edf44a61c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a0fc2b63b9a-0001-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We do not think that title III of the ADA was intended to apply extraterritorially."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1388",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a0fc2b63b9ac03869965db16cacd030a9987871042851b9b41a4a7edf44a61c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a0fc2b63b9a-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When -- when the ship is out on the high seas?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "David B. Salmons",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1388",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a0fc2b63b9ac03869965db16cacd030a9987871042851b9b41a4a7edf44a61c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a0fc2b63b9a-0001-0010",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "definition of commerce here is broader than it was and specifically refers to travel between the United States and foreign countries."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Frederick",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1388",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a0fc2b63b9ac03869965db16cacd030a9987871042851b9b41a4a7edf44a61c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a0fc2b63b9a-0001-0011",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This case is about congressional intent not congressional power."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1388",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a0fc2b63b9ac03869965db16cacd030a9987871042851b9b41a4a7edf44a61c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a0fc2b63b9a-0001-0013",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I'm asking about the U.S. law and policy which says no segregation, no discrimination in places of public accommodation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1388",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a0fc2b63b9ac03869965db16cacd030a9987871042851b9b41a4a7edf44a61c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a0fc2b63b9a-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "what percentage of its passengers are from the USA?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Frederick",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1388",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a0fc2b63b9ac03869965db16cacd030a9987871042851b9b41a4a7edf44a61c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a0fc2b63b9a-0002-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In the year 2000, the United States Government issued a report that contained an extensive appendix, which we've cited in our brief, that details in laborious detail the conflicts between land-based ADA standards and SOLAS."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1388",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a0fc2b63b9ac03869965db16cacd030a9987871042851b9b41a4a7edf44a61c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a0fc2b63b9a-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is that limited, though, just to things that affect the internal order of the ship?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1388",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a0fc2b63b9ac03869965db16cacd030a9987871042851b9b41a4a7edf44a61c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a0fc2b63b9a-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "there was no legal relationship of any sort between the supplier of the patent-infringing object and the ship in the United States."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Frederick",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1388",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a0fc2b63b9ac03869965db16cacd030a9987871042851b9b41a4a7edf44a61c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a0fc2b63b9a-0002-0007",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "there's an amicus brief written where there's only one or two stops in the United States a year, and under their view, that ship would be governed by the ADA as well."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Gregory G. Garre",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1388",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a0fc2b63b9ac03869965db16cacd030a9987871042851b9b41a4a7edf44a61c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a0fc2b63b9a-0002-0008",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Applying title III of the Americans With Disabilities Act to foreign-flagged vessels would invite precisely the sort of international discord, conflict, and confusion that Congress presumably seeks to avoid when it writes American laws."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1388",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a0fc2b63b9ac03869965db16cacd030a9987871042851b9b41a4a7edf44a61c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a0fc2b63b9a-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: What about the -- what about the full sweep argument? Let's sort of come full circle on that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1388",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a0fc2b63b9ac03869965db16cacd030a9987871042851b9b41a4a7edf44a61c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a0fc2b63b9a-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: What's -- what's the full sweep argument? I don't --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Garre",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1388",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a0fc2b63b9ac03869965db16cacd030a9987871042851b9b41a4a7edf44a61c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a0fc2b63b9a-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GARRE: Justice Souter, first of all, it's -- it -- the statute doesn't say full sweep. It says sweep, and that's in the findings of the ADA."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Garre",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1388",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a0fc2b63b9ac03869965db16cacd030a9987871042851b9b41a4a7edf44a61c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a0fc2b63b9a-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It's important to understand the -- the potential international conflicts that extending the ADA to foreign-flagged vessels could create. There are more than 40 nations that have adopted anti-discrimination laws for the disabled."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1388",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a0fc2b63b9ac03869965db16cacd030a9987871042851b9b41a4a7edf44a61c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a0fc2b63b9a-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: When you say different, you mean you cannot comply with both."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Garre",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1388",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a0fc2b63b9ac03869965db16cacd030a9987871042851b9b41a4a7edf44a61c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a0fc2b63b9a-0003-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We cite the 1996 guidelines in our brief. Those guidelines right now are -- are not binding guidelines, but they could well become binding guidelines."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Garre",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1388",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a0fc2b63b9ac03869965db16cacd030a9987871042851b9b41a4a7edf44a61c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a0fc2b63b9a-0003-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Bahamian Government has a solemn responsibility under international law and under its own law to govern the construction and design of all flags of all ships that fly -- fly its flags. Article 10 of the Geneva Convention on the High Seas recognizes that flag states have responsibility for the construction and design of ships."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Garre",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1388",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a0fc2b63b9ac03869965db16cacd030a9987871042851b9b41a4a7edf44a61c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a0fc2b63b9a-0003-0007",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And in the Brown v. Duchesne case, this Court recognized that, a case that dealt with the application of patent laws to the construction and design of a foreign-flagged vessels."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Garre",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1388",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a0fc2b63b9ac03869965db16cacd030a9987871042851b9b41a4a7edf44a61c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a0fc2b63b9a-0003-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And we would urge this Court to return this matter to Congress. Congress is in the position to weigh the risk of international confusion, to weigh the potential for international discord and to address those matters as it sees -- sees fit."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1388",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a0fc2b63b9ac03869965db16cacd030a9987871042851b9b41a4a7edf44a61c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a0fc2b63b9a-0003-0009",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
